1. Requirement Gathering & Analysis: Collecting and defining all client requirements and project scope.
2. System Design: Creating the software architecture, database design, and user interface workflows.
3. Implementation (Coding): Developers write the actual program code based on the design specifications.
4. Testing: QA engineers test the software to find defects and ensure expected performance.
5. Deployment: Releasing the verified application to the production server for end users.
6. Maintenance: Fixing issues, applying security patches, and enhancing the system after release.
